    L("sheshunoff_v_johnson.md", "Alex Sheshunoff Management Services, L.P. v. Johnson", "209 S.W.3d 644 (Tex. 2006)", "The Texas Supreme Court held that a covenant not to compete in an at-will employment agreement is enforceable when the employer's promise (e.g., to provide confidential information) is **performed**, even if not performed at the moment of contracting — **modifying *Light v. Centel Cellular* (1994)** to the extent *Light* required the consideration to be given at the time the agreement was made. The court emphasized that the core inquiry is the reasonableness of the restraint under §15.50.", kind="case law", verbatim=False)
